#: ../../source/docs/introduction.rst:5
#: 725ec0b5000b4535bb6e7c750925c3b8
msgid "Introduction to Plane"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/introduction.rst:7
#: 89aeb642f6ed47a1a68f0d3c3e784557
msgid "Plane is an advanced open-source autopilot firmware system for conventional planes, flying wings, and VTOL capable QuadPlanes.  It offers a :ref:`wide variety of flight modes <flight-modes>` from fully manual to fully autonomous."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/introduction.rst:11
#: e9fca5fddd084f77a795029d41af7e4c
msgid "As part of the wider ArduPilot software platform it works seamlessly with a variety of :ref:`Ground Control Station programs <common-GCS>` that are used to setup the vehicle, monitor the vehicle's flight in real-time and perform powerful mission planning activities. It also benefits from other parts of the ArduPilot ecosystem, including simulators, log analysis tools, and higher level APIs for vehicle control."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/introduction.rst:14
#: 914439d8d3704c54b3ea0199973f8478
msgid "ArduPilot is already a preferred software platform for numerous commercially available autopilot systems but you can also use it to enhance the abilities of your own DIY planes or convert normal RC only systems into fully featured autonomous aircraft."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/introduction.rst:16
#: 03dd3284929d406595902e6c9ce703cf
msgid "Please do not be tempted to skip over steps and rush into flight. This is robotics and aviation combined -- both of which are quite complex on their own. Take some time to become familiar with documentation. Follow the steps patiently, and you will get your vehicle safely up in the air."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/introduction.rst:22
#: c3d6f73b607b4450a7aca92dfbfca928
msgid ":ref:`Selecting an autopilot controller for your system <common-autopilots>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/introduction.rst:23
#: 4b986a1720d54e7480426da7b91414ce
msgid ":ref:`First Time Setup <arduplane-setup>`- Installing: hardware, software, and firmware. Plugging in: Sensors, radios, batteries, motors, etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/introduction.rst:24
#: 8607d63d079946efa6a7cbc25645d2e6
msgid ":ref:`Configuration <plane-configuration-landing-page>`- Designate control outputs for flying surfaces. Establish telemetry and control between: vehicle, ground-station, and RC-control transmitter. Set up flight modes, program failsafe behavior, calibrate sensors and motor-controllers, and verify correct motor operation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/introduction.rst:25
#: 9788752bd60842c5b429e4015c8c9510
msgid ":ref:`First Flight and Tuning <first-flight-landing-page>`- First test flight and tuning stabilization, and speed/height controller"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/introduction.rst:26
#: 3d9bbad3872a4d469e2dbcbc71bdf8d6
msgid ":ref:`Mission planning <common-mission-planning>` - Programming missions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/introduction.rst:31
#: 274d03ac177a46f4a02d4a3d8fa250b8
msgid "**The topic of safety should be foremost on your mind.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/introduction.rst:33
#: e08a97a9373341e8843f8dcfbd9f165c
msgid "**Autonomous vehicles are high-energy systems driving rotating blades -- you are in charge of these potential hazards.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/introduction.rst:38
#: aa5f4dc622bf424a96fe02d2717be115
msgid "*ArduPilot supported autopilots and peripherals are designed to easily integrate with most standard RC aircraft, from simple high-wing trainers to high-speed swept wing fighters and flying wings, to QuadPlane . If you have something out of the ordinary please assume that a bit more tuning will be required to get things dialed in.*"
msgstr ""

